{"shortDescription":"The forint eased to a six-week low on Wednesday, leading a retreat among central Europe's currencies, after Hungary's central bank renewed the possibility of an interest rate cut by the end of the year.Hungarian policymakers on Tuesday left their main rate at 5.50% but discussed a cut. Governor Mih…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The forint eased to a six-week low on Wednesday, leading a retreat among central Europe's currencies, after Hungary's central bank renewed the possibility of an interest rate cut by the end of the year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Hungarian policymakers on Tuesday left their main rate at 5.50% but discussed a cut. Governor Mihaly Varga said more favourable conditions had increased the bank's room to manoeuvre."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The likelihood that the central bank will cut interest rates in December has somewhat increased,\" Erste Group Bank analysts said."]},{"type":"p","children":["The forint ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX:EURHUF","text":"FX:EURHUF"}}," traded nearly 0.2% down at 367.25 to the euro at 0852 GMT, off a session low of 367.89."]},{"type":"p","children":["The National Bank of Hungary paused a string of rate cuts in September."]},{"type":"p","children":["Goldman Sachs reiterated weaker price developments would provide room for Hungary's easing campaign to resume and markets had overreacted to energy price concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"While elevated wholesale energy prices previously warranted caution on monetary policy, the sharp fall in oil prices in recent weeks (if maintained) should mitigate further inflationary concerns,\" Goldman Sachs said."]},{"type":"p","children":["DIVERGENT RATE PATHS"]},{"type":"p","children":["The Hungarian government's ambition to adopt the euro in the coming years, which propelled the forint to multi-year highs earlier this year, has been ballast in recent months as markets face turmoil from the war in the Middle East and the disruption to global energy markets."]},{"type":"p","children":["The forint is the only currency among regional peers to gain this year. And with rates already high, Hungary has been keen to bring borrowing costs down."]},{"type":"p","children":["In contrast, the Czech Republic has hiked rates twice this year, and Poland may follow by early next year to counter inflation pressures caused mainly by energy costs."]},{"type":"p","children":["On Tuesday, Poland's government said it would freeze gas prices at current levels for households in order to alleviate pressures stemming from the situation in the Middle East. Some analysts said that could reduce the likelihood of rate hikes."]},{"type":"p","children":["Poland's zloty ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURPLN","text":"OANDA:EURPLN"}}," and the Czech crown ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURCZK","text":"OANDA:EURCZK"}}," both eased 0.1% to 0.2%, in line with the forint. Stock markets were lower."]},{"type":"p","children":["Shares in Polish online broker XTB ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"GPW:XTB","text":"GPW:XTB"}}," continued to slump on Wednesday after falling over 17% on Tuesday following signals from Poland's financial watchdog KNF of a possible intervention on contracts for difference (CFDs), which drive the bulk of XTB's revenue."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":6},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT  0952 CET"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["CURRENCIES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-c